From aa775834b1ba47701160a0c5617649d1716c2746 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 23:20:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] xen-virtual-device: ship mac80211_hwsim so the guest can host
 shadow APs

virt_wifi can only ever synthesise one fake network called "VirtWifi", so AAOS's Wi-Fi
screen can never list real access points with it. The plan is to give the guest
mac80211_hwsim radios instead: wlan0 as the station AAOS uses, and further radios on
which hostapd beacons SSIDs mirrored from what DomD's real Wi-Fi actually sees, so the
user picks a genuine SSID on screen.

mac80211_hwsim, mac80211 and libarc4 were all built but left in _IMPLICIT_MODULES, i.e.
not distributed -- and the guest cannot load what the image does not ship. Confirmed on
the running DomA: /vendor_dlkm/lib/modules and /vendor/lib/modules contain neither
mac80211.ko nor mac80211_hwsim.ko, and lsmod showed no 802.11 stack at all. Move all
three to _VIRT_COMMON_MODULES, keeping the list in ASCII order. This is the same move
that was already made for virt_wifi/cfg80211/rfkill and proven to reach the guest.

No host-side component is needed. The .ko carries both transports, and with no virtio
hwsim device and no wmediumd netlink registrant present it falls back to its own
in-kernel "perfect channel medium" -- which is what matters here, because
neither qemu 7.0 nor qemu 10.0 has a virtio mac80211-hwsim device model (no file
matching hwsim in hw/ of either), so the
Cuttlefish arrangement of putting the APs in a separate VM is not available.

Radios are not created by the module: BOARD_KERNEL_CMDLINE already carries
mac80211_hwsim.radios=0, and /apex/com.google.cf.wifi/bin/mac80211_create_radios makes
them at runtime over the MAC80211_HWSIM genl family. That binary is already in the image
(com.google.cf.wifi.apex), as is hostapd (com.google.cf.wpa_supplicant.apex).

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending [yhamamachi/android_kernel_xen-virtual-device]
---
 BUILD.bazel | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
index 4e401c1..ceca6db 100644
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -61,6 +61,20 @@ filegroup(
 _VIRT_COMMON_MODULES = [
     "cfg80211.ko",
     "failover.ko",
+    # mac80211_hwsim simulates 802.11 radios inside the guest, so AAOS can be given a
+    # real cfg80211 station (wlan0) plus extra radios to run shadow APs on. Distributed
+    # rather than left implicit because the guest cannot load what the image does not
+    # ship: mac80211_hwsim needs mac80211, which needs libarc4.
+    #
+    # The module is loaded with radios=0 (BOARD_KERNEL_CMDLINE already carries
+    # mac80211_hwsim.radios=0) and the radios are created at runtime by
+    # /apex/com.google.cf.wifi/bin/mac80211_create_radios, the same way Cuttlefish does
+    # it. No host-side component is required: with no virtio hwsim device and no wmediumd
+    # netlink registrant the driver falls back to its own in-kernel "perfect channel
+    # medium", which is what the shadow APs ride on.
+    "libarc4.ko",
+    "mac80211.ko",
+    "mac80211_hwsim.ko",
     "net_failover.ko",
     "rfkill.ko",
     "rpmsg_ns.ko",
@@ -163,9 +177,6 @@ _IMPLICIT_MODULES = [
     "kunit.ko",
     "l2tp_core.ko",
     "l2tp_ppp.ko",
-    "libarc4.ko",
-    "mac80211.ko",
-    "mac80211_hwsim.ko",
     "mac802154.ko",
     "macsec.ko",
     "mii.ko",
